n 'check valid actions' and act on it (e.g., free a hand by leaving an object) instead of looping on planning text.", "When When the proposer emits planning-only 'think' statements or repeats actions instead of executing the needed manipulation, especially near the end of a multi-object transfer.: Stop supporting 'think' proposals; demand and verify a concrete executable action each step, and if progress stalls, run 'check valid actions' and act on it rather than looping on planning text."], 'finalizer': ['When When a block-stacking goal requires rearranging an existing tower whose base must be freed and rebuilt in a specific order.: First check valid actions to identify which block is actually movable, then unstack the blocking block to the table, rebuild the target tower bottom-up, and continue executing concrete pick/stack actions without redundant think steps.', 'When When both hands are occupied and the valid-action check shows only leave actions are available, further planning is useless until a hand is freed.: After checking valid actions, immediately execute the listed leave action rather than emitting more think steps; do not repeat planning once the next concrete action is known.', 'When When a repetitive multi-object transfer task has a known, working action pattern and the step budget is limited.: Once the transfer pattern is established, execute the concrete pick/move/drop actions directly and continuously without redundant think steps or duplicate moves, tracking remaining objects and cycling until all are delivered, since each redundant action consumes limited budget needed for the final transfers.']}
