d with a real manipulation rather than looping on planning text.', "When When the proposer keeps emitting only 'think' statements or repeats an action that the environment rejects, and when both hands are occupied blocking the needed manipulation.: Stop supporting repeated no-op 'think' proposals; demand a concrete executable action. After an invalid action, immediately run 'check valid actions' and act on it (e.g., free a hand by leaving an object) instead of looping on planning text."], 'finalizer': ['When When a block-stacking goal requires rearranging an existing tower whose base must be freed and rebuilt in a specific order.: Identify the movable block via valid actions, then immediately execute concrete unstack/putdown/pickup/stack actions to clear the base and rebuild the tower bottom-up, checking valid actions only when a move fails and avoiding redundant think steps that waste the step budget.', "When When a goal requires moving a specific object into a container but that object is not yet in the container and its location is unknown.: After a fetch-from-container action fails because the object isn't there, immediately run check valid actions to discover where the object can be obtained, then execute the concrete fetch/move action rather than emitting repeated think steps.", 'When When both hands are occupied and the valid-action check shows only leave actions are available, further planning is useless until a hand is freed.: After checking valid actions, immediately execute the listed leave action rather than emitting more think steps; do not repeat planning once the next concrete action is known.']}
